FileHunter is built on open-source libraries. The main ones:

  Tauri (app window)                          MIT / Apache-2.0
  iroh (encrypted peer connections)           MIT / Apache-2.0
  Apache OpenDAL (S3 storage)                 Apache-2.0
  tokio, reqwest, rustls (networking)         MIT / Apache-2.0 / ISC
  rayon (parallel disk scanning)              MIT / Apache-2.0
  BLAKE3 (file hashes)                        CC0-1.0 / Apache-2.0
  zstd (index compression)                    MIT / BSD-3-Clause
  SQLite via rusqlite (hash cache)            Public Domain / MIT
  notify (file change events)                 CC0-1.0 / MIT / Apache-2.0
  serde, bincode (data formats)               MIT / Apache-2.0
  trash (system Recycle Bin)                  MIT
  keyring (macOS Keychain)                    MIT / Apache-2.0

The full list of dependencies with versions is in Cargo.lock; license texts are
available in the respective projects' repositories.

Peer connections over the internet use public address-lookup and relay servers
run by n0 (the iroh project). They see only device IDs and encrypted data.
